.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1046 AM PDT Thu Sep 17 2026

Low clouds will gradually scatter out into the early afternoon
hours, giving way to VFR conditions across area terminals. Light
winds will increase this afternoon with a moderate onshore breeze
developing. The marine layer is anticipated to return this
evening. Latest models indicate the marine layer will compress
overnight resulting in lower cigs overnight into Friday.
Confidence is moderate with respect to timing and cig heights.

Vicinity of SFO... VFR cigs will gradually scatter out by the
afternoon, with a moderate onshore breeze developing in the
afternoon. Cigs will return this evening and persist through the
overnight hours, with moderate confidence in timing and ceilings
height.

SFO Bridge Approach... Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals... VFR cigs will scatter out by early
afternoon with a gentle west-northwest wind developing. Winds
will ease overnight becoming light and locally variable with low
clouds anticipated to return. Confidence in timing is moderate.

